From: YuZora kernel porter <kartik@aoisora.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] qcacmn: define __qdf_bug() when WLAN_DEBUG is off

drivers/staging/qcacld-3.0/core/hdd/src/wlan_hdd_assoc.o:
undefined reference to `__qdf_bug' (from qdf_lock.h:352,
cdp_txrx_ctrl.h:237, cdp_txrx_cmn.h:811) at the vmlinux link,
kernel build run #4, 2026-11-24, Gate 3.

Root cause: __qdf_bug() is defined only in
drivers/staging/qca-wifi-host-cmn/qdf/linux/src/qdf_trace.c, whose
whole body is wrapped in `#ifdef WLAN_DEBUG` (lines 25-3993,
added by commit d77419c, "qcacmn: Disable all of qdf_trace when
WLAN_DEBUG is disabled"). WLAN_DEBUG is only -D'd when
BUILD_DEBUG_VERSION=y (drivers/staging/qcacld-3.0/configs/
default_defconfig: BUILD_DEBUG_VERSION := n, the default). But
PANIC_ON_BUG=y, because CONFIG_SLUB_DEBUG=y (defconfig line 285
-> qcacld default_defconfig lines 514-521), so
i_qdf_trace.h takes the extern-declaration branch and QDF_BUG()
emits calls to __qdf_bug() — while the definition compiles to
nothing. The run #4 log proves it: qdf_trace.o WAS compiled (log
line 4690) yet provides no __qdf_bug.

Fix: define __qdf_bug() after the closing `#endif /* WLAN_DEBUG
*/`, guarded by exactly the same condition as the header's extern
branch (PANIC_ON_BUG + CONFIG_SLUB_DEBUG) plus !WLAN_DEBUG, so it
cannot duplicate the original definition when WLAN_DEBUG is on.
Same body as the original (BUG(); + qdf_export_symbol). No
behaviour change in a debug build; a non-debug build with
PANIC_ON_BUG now links instead of failing.

CORRECTION 2026-11-24 (run #5 failed on the first version of this
patch — "patch does not apply" at qdf_trace.c:3991): the first
version was written against a reconstruction of the file that
ended at line 3993, but the real file at the pinned commit ends
with a trailing blank line (line 3994). A hunk whose old side ends
at the file's last line in the reconstruction does not apply to a
file with one more line after it. This version was regenerated
from the real file (raw read at 4d83f24b) and verified with
`git apply --check` against that exact file before upload.

CORRECTION 2, 2026-11-24 (run #6 failed on the corrected version
— Gate 3, "4 errors generated", qdf_trace.c:4005-4009): the
appended definition was bare after the closing `#endif /*
WLAN_DEBUG */`, but every #include in this file sits INSIDE that
guard, so the appended block compiled with no declarations at
all: implicit declaration of BUG(), no previous prototype for
__qdf_bug (-Wmissing-prototypes), and qdf_export_symbol undefined
(declaration specifier missing). This version makes the block
self-contained: its own `#include <linux/bug.h>` +
`#include <linux/export.h>`, a forward declaration of __qdf_bug,
and the kernel's EXPORT_SYMBOL directly (qdf_export_symbol is a
qdf macro from headers compiled out here). Same guard, same body,
same hunk anchor as the version that applied cleanly in run #6.

Applies to kkisdevil/android_kernel_samsung_sm7150 @ 4d83f24b
(crDroid 4.14.357-openela). Applied porter-side by the
build-kernel workflow (patches/kernel/*.patch) so the pinned
kernel ref stays untouched.
---
diff --git a/drivers/staging/qca-wifi-host-cmn/qdf/linux/src/qdf_trace.c b/drivers/staging/qca-wifi-host-cmn/qdf/linux/src/qdf_trace.c
index 9651756..20c860e 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/qca-wifi-host-cmn/qdf/linux/src/qdf_trace.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/qca-wifi-host-cmn/qdf/linux/src/qdf_trace.c
@@ -3992,3 +3992,33 @@ qdf_export_symbol(__qdf_bug);
 #endif /* PANIC_ON_BUG */
 #endif /* WLAN_DEBUG */
 
+/*
+ * __qdf_bug() must be defined whenever QDF_BUG() can emit a call to
+ * it (i_qdf_trace.h takes the extern declaration when PANIC_ON_BUG
+ * and CONFIG_SLUB_DEBUG are both set), even when WLAN_DEBUG is off
+ * and the rest of this file is compiled out (BUILD_DEBUG_VERSION=n,
+ * the default). Without this, vmlinux fails to link with undefined
+ * reference to `__qdf_bug'. The !WLAN_DEBUG guard keeps this from
+ * duplicating the definition above when WLAN_DEBUG is on.
+ *
+ * CORRECTION 2026-11-24 (run #6, Gate 3, "4 errors generated"):
+ * the previous version appended the definition bare after the
+ * closing WLAN_DEBUG #endif, but every #include in this file sits
+ * INSIDE that guard, so the appended block had no declarations:
+ * BUG() implicitly declared, __qdf_bug with no prototype, and
+ * qdf_export_symbol undefined. This version brings its own
+ * includes plus a forward declaration and uses the kernel's
+ * EXPORT_SYMBOL directly (qdf_export_symbol is a qdf macro from
+ * headers compiled out here), so the block is self-contained.
+ */
+#if defined(PANIC_ON_BUG) && defined(CONFIG_SLUB_DEBUG) && !defined(WLAN_DEBUG)
+#include <linux/bug.h>
+#include <linux/export.h>
+
+void __qdf_bug(void);
+void __qdf_bug(void)
+{
+	BUG();
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL(__qdf_bug);
+#endif
